{
 "id": "arnio-pr2017",
 "repo": "im-anishraj/arnio",
 "base_ref": "v1.20.0",
 "base_commit": "2e3fe965c963d45ae156c32ef230c7eb7a29a777",
 "issue": 1682,
 "issue_title": "Bug: serialize mixed-type schema allowed values deterministically",
 "issue_body": "## Summary\n\n`Schema.to_json()` can crash when a field's `allowed` set contains mixed scalar types, because the serializer tries to sort the set directly.\n\n## Why it matters\n\n`String(allowed=...)` is typed as accepting `Any` values, and mixed scalar allow-lists can be valid for messy CSV validation. Serialization should either preserve those schemas safely or reject them at construction time with a clear error. A raw sort comparison error makes schema export unreliable.\n\n## Evidence\n\n- `arnio/schema.py`: `_normalize_sequence()` converts sets with `sorted(value)`.\n- Python cannot sort sets containing incomparable types such as `int` and `str`.\n- `Schema.to_json()` calls `_field_to_json_dict()`, which eventually normalizes `field_def.allowed` through this helper.\n\n## Reproduction or trigger\n\n```python\nimport arnio as ar\n\nschema = ar.Schema({\n    \"code\": ar.String(allowed={1, \"1\"}),\n})\n\nschema.to_json()\n```\n\n## Expected behavior\n\nSchema serialization should produce stable JSON for supported allowed values, or schema construction should reject mixed-type allowed values with a clear error.\n\n## Actual behavior\n\n`Schema.to_json()` raises a raw Python sorting error:\n\n```text\nTypeError: '<' not supported between instances of 'str' and 'int'\n```\n\n## Suggested direction\n\nUse a JSON-safe deterministic ordering strategy that does not compare raw mixed types, for example sorting by `(type(value).__name__, repr(value))`, or explicitly validate allowed values to a narrower supported type set. Add tests for:\n\n- homogeneous string allowed values\n- homogeneous numeric allowed values\n- mixed scalar allowed values\n- round-tripping through `Schema.to_json()` / `Schema.from_json()`\n\n## References\n\n- `arnio/schema.py::_normalize_sequence`\n- `arnio/schema.py::Schema.to_json`\n- `tests/test_schema.py`\n- `tests/test_schema_export.py`\r\n",
 "issue_url": "https://github.com/im-anishraj/arnio/issues/1682",
 "pr": 2017,
 "pr_title": "fix: deterministic sort for mixed-type allowed values",
 "pr_body": "Fixes #1682\r\n\r\n`_normalize_sequence()` called `sorted(value)` directly on sets, which raises `TypeError` when the set contains mixed scalar types like `{1, \"1\"}` since Python can't compare `int` and `str` with `<`.\r\n\r\nReplaced with a type-safe key:\r\n\r\n```python\r\nsorted(value, key=lambda x: (type(x).__name__, repr(x)))\r\n```\r\n\r\nTests added for homogeneous strings, homogeneous numerics, mixed scalars, and `to_json()` / `from_json()` round-trip.",
 "fix_commit": "121f1216eec95f58ca4e9a6e12ba23211deb53b6",
 "merged_at": "2026-05-29T13:16:41Z",
